{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && cat > update.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Eleventh turn: promotes the persistent-backend half of the measured failure into durable knowledge with its exact sources, and retargets the two open decision-formation questions to the cases the next retained run will cover (batched mixed proposals and leader-change adoption). The contrast receipt showed the persistent backend returning an error for the same below-compaction request and the core's own expect raising the abort, which is reusable knowledge for any other path that reads below a compacted index.\\\",\n  \\\"sources\\\": [\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"persistent_suffix\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos_storage/src/persistent_storage.rs\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 336, \\\"end_line\\\": 360, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"logsync_expect\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos/src/sequence_paxos/mod.rs\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 419, \\\"end_line\\\": 431, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"ref\\\": \\\"@persistent_below_compaction_error\\\",\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"behavior\\\",\n      \\\"statement\\\": \\\"\"'`PersistentStorage::get_suffix(from)` delegates to `get_entries(from, next_log_key)`, which returns an empty vector only for `to > next_log_key || from >= to`; otherwise it seeks to the first surviving key and reads `to - from` values consecutively, so a request below the compacted index runs past the last stored key and the missing value yields `Err(ErrHelper)`. The captured storage therefore returns an error instead of the empty vector the `Storage::get_suffix` contract specifies, and the core applies `expect(READ_ERROR_MSG)` to that result at sequence_paxos/mod.rs:428, which is the abort observed for the persistent-backend case.\",\n      \"conditions\": \"Captured snapshot; `get_suffix`/`get_entries` called with `from` below the compacted index while keys above it still exist; reached through `InternalStorage::get_suffix` from `create_log_sync`.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\"persistent_suffix\", \"storage_get_suffix_contract\", \"logsync_expect\"],\n      \"executions\": {\"5ffdf2f10d3943d39f56133f08c42a6e\": [8]},\n      \"knowledge\": [\n        {\"entry_id\": \"b2606c6f3c1148c5af396ef701166e6f-knowledge-0\", \"revision\": 1, \"assertion\": \"the non-snapshot branch reads get_suffix(common_prefix_idx) with no comparison against the responder'\"'s compacted index\\\"}\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"investigations\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"5d087c25407e4157b6b06176a649ef5c-question-0\\\",\n      \\\"discriminator\\\": \\\"Run a three-node in-process cluster with batch_size 4 where entries are proposed concurrently on the leader and on a follower, drive it until every node's decided index reaches the total, then compare the three decided vectors element by element and check that the entry readable at each index equals the vector element at that index. A mismatch would show the batched accept path reporting an index inconsistent with the entries a node holds.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"5d087c25407e4157b6b06176a649ef5c-question-1\\\",\n      \\\"discriminator\\\": \\\"In the same harness, decide a prefix, remove the leader, elect a replacement among the survivors, propose further entries, then recover the old leader from its persisted storage and compare every node's decided vector with the pre-change prefix: an unchanged prefix plus identical full vectors bounds the adoption path, while a changed or shortened prefix would show LogSync/AcceptSync truncating or reordering decided entries.\\\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nJSON\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
